From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve horizontal flips for negative odd echo orientations

Follow MilkDrop2 milkdropfs.cpp echo orientation nonzero signed remainder.
Finite negative odd orientations flip U just like positive odd values.
Preserve signed modulo4, V predicate, valid-input guards, zoom, mix,
gamma-only/echo epsilon distinctions and current float diffuse policy.
No pass, vertex, allocation or additional draw is introduced.

Original source: milkdrop2 f05b0d8, vis_milk2/milkdropfs.cpp.

---
diff --git a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp
index 99d5f00a1..a1dd06a6c 100644
--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/VideoEcho.cpp
@@ -139,7 +139,7 @@ void VideoEcho::DrawVideoEcho(const PerFrameContext& perFrameContext)
         {
             for (int vertex = 0; vertex < 4; vertex++)
             {
-                if (videoEchoOrientation % 2 == 1)
+                if (videoEchoOrientation % 2 != 0)
                 {
                     m_echoMesh.UVs()[vertex].SetU(1.0f - m_echoMesh.UVs()[vertex].U());
                 }
